{"type":"assistant","uuid":"c4ccdd57-f9ea-4563-b89c-b885aee1c381","session_id":"92340c90-20bf-4317-b14e-4e56be5fd9d8","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"c4ccdd57-f9ea-4563-b89c-b885aee1c381","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe bug is fixed. Here's a summary:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Bug:** Crash (`NumberFormatException`) when entering numbers larger than `Integer.MAX_VALUE` or `Long.MAX_VALUE` in the TOTP/HOTP manual entry dialog.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `ManualEntryDialog` class used `Integer.parseInt()` and `Long.parseLong()` directly on user input without any bounds checking. When a number exceeded the type's maximum value, a `NumberFormatException` was thrown, crashing the app.\n\n**Fix (saved to `bug-1215-fix.patch`):**\n\n1. **Added two safe parsing helpers:**\n   - `safeParseInt(String)` — returns `-1` on overflow instead of throwing\n   - `safeParseLong(String)` — returns `-1L` on overflow instead of throwing\n\n2. **Updated the Save button onClick handler** to:\n   - Use `safeParseInt`/`safeParseLong` instead of direct parsing for `digits`, `period`, and `counter`\n   - Add overflow checks (`< 0`) that silently `return` from onClick, preventing the save and avoiding the crash\n\n3. **Updated the TextWatcher** to:\n   - Use safe parsing for `digits`, `period`, and `counter` validation\n   - Add overflow checks (`< 0`) that disable the Save button when invalid values are entered\n\n**Result:** Entering an out-of-range number will now disable the Save button in real-time (via the TextWatcher), and the save operation will safely return without crashing (via the onClick overflow checks).\n\n**Verification:** `./gradlew clean assembleDebug` — BUILD SUCCESSFUL (both `fdroidDebug` and `playDebug` variants)"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":57360,"output_tokens":374,"cache_read_input_tokens":55968,"total_tokens":57734}}}
